K.  PASS/FAIL on the headline quantity: engine A electron yield
==============================================================================
   engine A / SvS85, H I, z = 10, 300 eV - 3 keV
     x_e = 1e-04 : 0.9499 - 0.9644   ok
     x_e = 1e-03 : 0.9865 - 1.0019   ok
     x_e = 1e-02 : 0.9506 - 1.0190   ok
     x_e = 1e-01 : 0.6906 - 0.9426   (excluded: SvS85 limiting fits degrade)
   PASS

   NOT COVERED BY ANY PASS/FAIL BLOCK -- reported, not asserted:
     * the H I / He I SPLIT.  Engine A gives f_HeI/f_HI -> 0.0871 at
       high energy; SvS85 Table 2 gives 0.0784 at their n_He/n_H = 0.1,
       i.e. 0.0637 rescaled to the Planck 0.08130.  The two differ by
       37 per cent.  No tolerance is asserted because SvS85's
       helium fits assume x_HeII = x_HII, which contradicts the
       fully-neutral helium used here; the disagreement is a stated
       systematic of the helium branch, not a test that passed.
     * the species split is INSENSITIVE to the shape of Lambda:
       tripling the helium term moves f_HeI by 2.8 per cent at 100 eV and
       < 0.2 per cent above 1 keV, which is the derivation's own claim.
     * the PHOTON emissivity normalisations (Gaikwad+23,
       Giovinazzo+26) are inputs, not outputs: nothing here can
       falsify them.

