J.  Tueros et al. (2014) benchmark, their Eq. (2)
==============================================================================
   I_Ec = E_c Int I(E) E^-beta dE / Int E^(1-beta) dE,
   beta = 2.2, E1 = 1 MeV, E2 = 100 TeV, E_c = 1 MeV, z_inj = 19.
   (integration capped at 1e+13 eV, engine A's ceiling)
     A-csda (this work, z=20)               I_1MeV = 9.381e+02
     A-transport (z=20)                     I_1MeV = 8.199e+03
     W = 36 eV, no IC losses (their I_H)    I_1MeV = 2.778e+04
     Tueros et al. (2014) quote             I_1MeV = 1.500e+04

   The 'no IC losses' row brackets their value to within a factor
   1.9, which is consistent with block H: their CMB energy density
   is low enough that inverse Compton barely removes energy from the
   cascade, whereas engine A cools the electron on the measured CMB.

